{"step_index":185,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T12:08:15Z","thinking":"**Addressing missing variable values**\n\nThe `--check` mode prevents actual file copying, leading to undefined destination and checksum in the result. The current implementation uses undefined variables in those cases. The variables are currently being set to empty in the `copy-to-tmp.yml` task. This task currently does not handle those undefined variables properly. Therefore, default values should be applied to prevent errors when the file is not copied in check mode. The fix involves using `copy_result.dest | default(target_dest)` and `copy_result.checksum | default('N/A')` to ensure these variables are always populated with suitable defaults, preventing errors.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"cat << 'EOF' > /home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/copy-to-tmp.yml\\n---\\n- name: Validate local source file\\n  hosts: localhost\\n  connection: local\\n  gather_facts: false\\n  tasks:\\n    - name: Validate that src_file parameter is provided\\n      ansible.builtin.fail:\\n        msg: >-\\n          Missing required variable 'src_file'.\\n          Usage: ansible-playbook playbooks/copy-to-tmp.yml -e \\\"src_file=/path/to/file\\\"\\n      when: src_file is not defined or src_file | length == 0\\n\\n    - name: Verify source file exists on control machine\\n      ansible.builtin.stat:\\n        path: \\\"{{ src_file }}\\\"\\n      register: local_src_stat\\n\\n    - name: Fail if source file does not exist on control machine\\n      ansible.builtin.fail:\\n        msg: \\\"Source file '{{ src_file }}' does not exist on Debian Trixie control node.\\\"\\n      when: not local_src_stat.stat.exists\\n\\n- name: Copy file to remote /tmp directory\\n  hosts: all\\n  gather_facts: false\\n  vars:\\n    target_filename: \\\"{{ dest_filename | default(src_file | basename) }}\\\"\\n    target_dest: \\\"/tmp/{{ target_filename }}\\\"\\n\\n  tasks:\\n    - name: Copy file to remote /tmp directory\\n      ansible.builtin.copy:\\n        src: \\\"{{ src_file }}\\\"\\n        dest: \\\"{{ target_dest }}\\\"\\n        mode: \\\"{{ dest_mode | default('0644') }}\\\"\\n        backup: \\\"{{ dest_backup | default(false) }}\\\"\\n      register: copy_result\\n\\n    - name: Report file transfer summary\\n      ansible.builtin.debug:\\n        msg:\\n          - \\\"Host: {{ inventory_hostname }}\\\"\\n          - \\\"Destination: {{ copy_result.dest | default(target_dest) }}\\\"\\n          - \\\"State: {{ 'CHANGED (new/updated file copied)' if copy_result.changed else 'OK (file already identical in /tmp)' }}\\\"\\n          - \\\"Checksum: {{ copy_result.checksum | default('N/A') }}\\\"\\nEOF\\nansible-lint /home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/copy-to-tmp.yml && ansible-playbook -i \\\"127.0.0.1,\\\" playbooks/copy-to-tmp.yml -c local -e \\\"src_file=/home/koby/.ansible/ansible.cfg\\\" --check\\n\"","Cwd":"\"/home/koby/.ansible\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Running command\"","toolSummary":"\"Test updated copy-to-tmp playbook\""}}]}
