{"step_index":209,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T12:10:30Z","content":"I've created both the production-grade Ansible playbook and the automation script in your **[~/.ansible](file:///home/koby/.ansible)** workspace.\n\n---\n\n### What Was Built\n\n#### 1. Playbook: [playbooks/copy-to-tmp.yml](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/copy-to-tmp.yml)\n- **Role**: Safely transfers any specified local file to `/tmp/` on the remote host.\n- **Validation**: Verifies that the source file exists on your Debian Trixie control node before connecting.\n- **Idempotency**: Uses `ansible.builtin.copy` (reports <span style=\"color:green\">OK</span> if identical, <span style=\"color:yellow\">CHANGED</span> if updated).\n- **Standards**: Passed `ansible-lint` with a **5/5-star production profile**.\n\n#### 2. Automation Script: [scripts/copy-to-remote.sh](file:///home/koby/.ansible/scripts/copy-to-remote.sh)\n*(Also symlinked at `~/.ansible/copy-to-remote.sh` for convenience)*\n- **Step 1 (Inspection)**: Tests if `koby-bowser-ansible` already has passwordless SSH access to the remote host using your Debian Trixie Ed25519 key ([~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub](file:///home/koby/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub), `koby@debian-trixie`).\n- **Step 2 (Bootstrap on demand)**: If the user is missing or passwordless login fails:\n  - Connects using the admin user (default `root`, or via `-a <admin_user>`).\n  - Creates system account `koby-bowser-ansible` with `/bin/bash` shell.\n  - Grants passwordless sudo in `/etc/sudoers.d/koby-bowser-ansible` (`0440`).\n  - Sets up `~/.ssh/authorized_keys` with strict permissions (`0700`/`0600`) and inserts your Debian Trixie public key.\n  - Re-verifies passwordless authentication.\n- **Step 3 (Playbook Execution)**: Invokes `ansible-playbook` passing the specified file in the command to save it to `/tmp`.\n\n#### 3. Workspace Quality-of-Life\n- Configured `.vault_pass` (`0600`) in [ansible.cfg](file:///home/koby/.ansible/ansible.cfg), resolving the known Ansible gotcha where `playbooks/group_vars/all/vault.yml` previously demanded vault decryption on unrelated plays.\n\n---\n\n### How to Use\n\n#### Method A: Run Everything in One Shot (via Script)\n\nFrom your `~/.ansible` directory:\n\n```bash\n./scripts/copy-to-remote.sh <REMOTE_HOST> <FILE_PATH>\n```\n\n**Common Examples:**\n\n```bash\n# Standard SSH (port 22, root bootstrap if needed)\n./scripts/copy-to-remote.sh 192.168.1.50 /home/koby/sample.txt\n\n# Custom SSH port (e.g. port 30) with custom admin user for initial provisioning\n./scripts/copy-to-remote.sh -p 30 -a admin srv-prod.lan /home/koby/config.tar.gz\n```\n\n> **Terminal Colors to Watch For**:\n> - <span style=\"color:green\">**Green `[OK]`**</span>: User `koby-bowser-ansible` is present and verified with passwordless authentication.\n> - <span style=\"color:yellow\">**Yellow `[INFO]`**</span>: User missing or unauthenticated; the script automatically provisions the account.\n> - <span style=\"color:blue\">**Blue command output**</span>: Real-time Ansible playbook execution.\n> - <span style=\"color:green\">**Green `[SUCCESS]`**</span>: File successfully saved into remote `/tmp`.\n\n---\n\n#### Method B: Execute the Playbook Directly via Ansible\n\nOnce `koby-bowser-ansible` is configured on the target host:\n\n```bash\nansible-playbook -i \"<REMOTE_HOST>,\" playbooks/copy-to-tmp.yml \\\n  -u koby-bowser-ansible \\\n  -e \"src_file=/home/koby/sample.txt\"\n```\n\n*(Optional overrides: `-e \"dest_filename=renamed.txt\"`, `-e \"dest_mode=0755\"`, `-e \"dest_backup=true\"`)*","thinking":"**Confirming Configuration Completeness**\n\nThe configuration appears complete, with the defined playbook. The playbook focuses on validating the source file's existence and then securely copying it to a temporary location with appropriate permissions and backup options. It is designed to return structured details, including checksum information to verify the file integrity.\n\n\n"}
